Refactor this code by memoizing the slow scoring function called with repeated inputs:

def score(pair):
    time.sleep(0.2)
    return model.similarity(pair[0], pair[1])

def rank(pairs):
    return sorted(pairs, key=score)

output:
from functools import lru_cache

@lru_cache(maxsize=None)
def score(left, right):
    time.sleep(0.2)
    return model.similarity(left, right)

def rank(pairs):
    return sorted(pairs, key=lambda p: score(*p))

What changed: score now takes hashable arguments so the cache key works; duplicate pairs across sorts hit the cache instead of sleeping again.

